<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108594" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκόλπ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lying on the bosom, in the
				lap,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλος τοι γλυκίων ὑποκόλπιος;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					14.37
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐραστὴν . . ἔχονθ᾽ ὑποκόλπιον ἄλλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.129
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Maec.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				274
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυδίλλης
			ὑποκόλπιος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>worn</i> or <i>concealed in the fold of the robe,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξίφη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					7.11.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιβλίδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.208
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>in the mother's womb,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλων ὑποκόλπιος αἰνὰ χολώθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Del.</u>
					86
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
